Start S-PLUS

rm(.Random.seed)
runif(1)
q()

Next time you start up, this should be fine.

.Random.seed is an S object, and it has got corrupted.  Tht should give
you a new copy unless your .Data directory is really messed up (when you
would need to move it to a safe place and start again).

