Dear Alesia

What you can do is using the CallBackFunction argument in the gui
FunctionInfo. This provides computation, updating of dialogs and inteaction
with datasetsin the GUI invironment (the call back function is just
something like "if you bush a "get" buttom,you can set s-plus to get
something). Now, you can actually use this call back function to initialize
the GUI dialog. Hereby you can initialse a combo box, or a selection list
by using parse arguments. What I mean is: find all lists available in your
chapter (use

>a <- list(x=1)
>b <- data.frame(x=1)
> objects(where = 1, classes = "list")
[1] "a"
> objects(where = 1, classes = "data.frame")
[1] "b"

A good example of how to use callbackfunctions is given by the "propcomm"
S-PLUS script file (see the splus6/sample/dialogs library). Hre you will
finde something useful, namely

propcommCallBack <- function(df)
{
   dfIn <<- df  # Assign to a global variable for debugging purpose

   if(IsInitDialogMessage(df)) # Am I called to initialize the properties?
   {
 .
 .
.
}}

