From jean_adams at usgs.gov  Mon Jul 22 18:54:02 2002
From: jean_adams at usgs.gov (Jean V Adams)
Date: Mon, 22 Jul 2002 14:54:02 -0400
Subject: Summary: summary statistics for k-nearest neighbors
Message-ID: <OF9BC02D41.3A1D5328-ON85256BFE.0067A1DD@er.usgs.gov>

Thanks to David Paul for his helpful reply.
I came up with the following function which meets my needs.
See original posting below.

JVA

knnsumry <- function(train, test, z, k=2, FUN=mean) {
    ntrain <- dim(train)[1]
    ntest <- dim(test)[1]
    results <- numeric(ntest)
    for(i in 1:ntest) {
        dif <- train - test[rep(i, ntrain), ]
        dst <- sqrt(apply(dif^2, 1, sum))
        results[i] <- FUN(z[dst <= sort(dst)[k]])
        }
    results
    }

