> However, splus does not handle such tables (see help file: The total
> number of counts in the cross-classification table cannot be greater
> than 200).

For the 2x2 case, I have a script that might help:

fisher <- function(x,a=x[1,1],b=x[1,2],c=x[2,1],d=x[2,2]) {
  #       a | b
  #  x = -------
  #       c | d
  N <- sum(x)
  p <- dhyper(a,a+b,c+d,a+c)
  x <- seq(max(0,a+b-(N-a-c)),min(a+b,a+c))
  phyp <- dhyper(x,a+b,c+d,a+c)
  sum(phyp[phyp<p])+p
}

> xx <- matrix(c(1, 4, 49999, 49996), 2, 2)
> fisher(xx)
[1] 0.2187406
> yy <- matrix(c(7, 2, 6, 9), 2, 2)
> fisher.test(yy)

        Fisher's exact test

data:  yy 
p-value = 0.1049 
alternative hypothesis: two.sided 

> fisher(yy)
[1] 0.1049266

> 
> Is there any way (eg other software) to use fisher exact on such
> tables.

StatXact and LogXact might help for larger tables.

http://www.cytel.com/

Regards,

Sundar

