On Sun, 28 Jul 2002, Erin Hodgess wrote:

> I tried Prof. Ripley's kind suggestions, but am obtaining
> duplicate results with both the contr.sum and contr. poly
> contrasts.  What am I doing wrong, please?  Does anything
> appear obvious?

The first contrast is the same (up to a scale factor), so they
will be the same.

Note my caveat: these are Type 1 SSq's, so fitted sequentially.
The second column is fitted after adjusting for the first (and so on, in
general).  Only if the contrasts are orthogonal will you get
order-independent results.  (Note, order in model.matrix, not in the
split list.)

